# The vendored schema artifacts are byte-exact copies of a pinned spec commit,
# and PIN.json records a sha256 over those bytes which the corpus checks before
# using either one. Git's end-of-line translation would rewrite them on
# checkout — on Windows the LF blobs come back as CRLF — so the digest fails
# and the pin reports tampering where there was none. `-text` turns that
# translation off and nothing else.
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose. The repository-root .gitattributes is a
# trigger path for the MCP 2026 JSON-RPC id conformance lane, which is unrelated
# to this corpus; a nested file carries the same rule without pulling that lane
# into every change here.
#
# Deliberately not `-whitespace`. These files end with a blank line, exactly as
# upstream publishes them, and `git diff --check` reporting that is a fact worth
# keeping visible rather than a warning worth suppressing.
schema-*.json -text
